      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Orb states: transmitter (load: big, centered, parts turning, link ring) → docked (site: bottom-right, the moth in his tank) → field down (game: tank empty, stick steers) → recall (beam in, field up, a pulse)."
    },
    {
      "id": "k-buttons",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "Controls as decided on Responsive: stick (site: dial sections · game: steer, rim = thruster), tap the stick = button 1 (next entry, LAUNCH · tie silk / let go), ring top = button 2 (previous entry · recall), side ? = Cori."
    },
    {
      "id": "h-tank",
      "kind": "decision",
      "text": "The tank is the stick disc: where your thumb presses to move. The moth just happens to live there and swims about at random; he doesn't follow the stick. In the game the field drops and the plain stick shows (kit ss-orb: field vs stick layers).",
      "why": "User, 2026-11-22: \"just random, he just happens to be in a tank, and that tank is where they press their thumb to move.\""
